Subject: [PATCH] Let a peer load its own staged core instead of receiving it

A peer already supports a local core: distribution::peer takes the path from
--core, leases the cache entry, and verify_local_core rejects a core whose
signed envelope, model, tensor-parallel size or cluster export differs from
rank zero's. The agent passes such a path only when the grant names this node as
the core's source, and the controller names exactly one holder, so in practice
every peer receives its ranges from rank zero at launch even when orbit push has
already staged that rank's directory on the node.

This adds a per-member staged flag. The controller sets it when the node's
STATUS reports that rank's staged directory verified, and the agent then starts
the rank from its own path. Rank zero keeps distributing whatever a peer cannot
supply, so partial staging stays correct.

The saving lands on the source node: with every peer staged, rank zero no longer
needs the other ranks' payloads for a launch, which is about two thirds of a
three-rank core.
---
diff --git a/flare-cli/src/orbit/agent.rs b/flare-cli/src/orbit/agent.rs
index 642c08fc..f9c6a18f 100644
--- a/flare-cli/src/orbit/agent.rs
+++ b/flare-cli/src/orbit/agent.rs
@@ -1406,6 +1406,14 @@ fn run(agent: &Arc<Agent>, request: &Value) -> Result<Arc<Group>, Failure> {
             .source
             .as_ref()
             .is_some_and(|source| source.public_key == mine.to_hex());
+    // A rank whose staged directory the controller verified loads its own copy; rank zero
+    // then distributes only what a peer cannot supply.
+    let local_core = local_core
+        || grant
+            .members
+            .iter()
+            .find(|member| member.rank == rank)
+            .is_some_and(|member| member.staged);
     if local_core && !core.is_file() {
         return Err(format!("core {} is not on this node", core.display()).into());
     }
diff --git a/flare-cli/src/orbit/controller.rs b/flare-cli/src/orbit/controller.rs
index f6e1f5af..10ba5321 100644
--- a/flare-cli/src/orbit/controller.rs
+++ b/flare-cli/src/orbit/controller.rs
@@ -1361,6 +1361,16 @@ impl Controller {
                     public_key: node.public_key.clone(),
                     address: node.address.clone(),
                     gpus: placements[rank].clone(),
+                    staged: core
+                        .needs
+                        .rank_directories
+                        .get(rank)
+                        .is_some_and(|directory| {
+                            statuses[rank]
+                                .cores
+                                .iter()
+                                .any(|p| p.verified && &p.name == directory)
+                        }),
                 })
                 .collect(),
             rendezvous,
diff --git a/flare-cli/src/orbit/grant.rs b/flare-cli/src/orbit/grant.rs
index 354ad8fe..bf9e72dd 100644
--- a/flare-cli/src/orbit/grant.rs
+++ b/flare-cli/src/orbit/grant.rs
@@ -64,6 +64,11 @@ pub struct Member {
     /// UUIDs of the GPUs the rank uses on its node; empty leaves the choice to the rank.
     #[serde(default)]
     pub gpus: Vec<String>,
+    /// The node holds this rank's staged directory, so the rank loads that copy instead of
+    /// receiving its ranges from rank zero. Absent from a grant signed before this field
+    /// existed, which keeps an older grant launching as it did.
+    #[serde(default)]
+    pub staged: bool,
 }
 
 /// Where a node-held core lives: the node's public key and the primary file's absolute path.
